ST_S2BaseGameLocalization.sid_tutorialnotes_tutorial_note_backpack:
All picked up items are stored in the backpack. To open it, use <input>.

General controls:
<input> - turn gear panel on/off;
<input> - turn item description on/off;
<input> - turn automatic item comparing on/off;
<input> - select different item for comparing;
<input> - sort inventory.

Item controls:
<input> - open item menu;
<input> - uninstall all modules (for weapons only);
<input> - unload (for weapons only);
<input> - throw item away;
<input> - close inventory.

Sometimes, you have too many items in your backpack. An overloaded backpack wastes stamina and limits movements. You can get rid of the extra weight by throwing some inventory items away or selling them to the Merchant.

ST_S2BaseGameLocalization.sid_tutorialnotes_tutorial_note_compass_:
The compass serves as the main navigation tool, so that you don’t have to constantly look at your PDA. Not only it shows directions, but always has information on stalkers nearby, as well as corpses, stashes and other markers of the Map.

Main compass markers:
<image> - Main quest;
<image> - Side quest;
<image> - Enemy;
<image> - Target that has to be eliminated within this quest;
<image> - Corpse.

Marker display depends on whether it is being tracked on the PDA:
<image> - Quest tracked;
<image> - Quest not tracked.

The compass also shows markers from the map on your PDA:
<image><image><image><image><image> - custom marks;
<image> - Camp;
<image> - Merchant;
<image> - Technician;
<image> - Medic;
<image> - Guide;
<image> - Bed or a place to rest;
<image> - Personal stash;
<image> - Location;
<image> - Signal source;
<image> - Archanomaly.

